he attributes of the 'Item' class." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"220" height=
=3D"180" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=3D"1" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/i=
mages/courses/object-oriented-design-interview/grocery-store-system/image-9=
-2-I76WBLE6.svg" style=3D"color: transparent;"></div></figure>
<h4 id=3D"catalog">Catalog</h4>
<p>The Catalog class is responsible for maintaining a structured list of al=
l available products, each uniquely identified by a barcode. It provides me=
thods to add, update, remove, and retrieve items.</p>
<p>The UML diagram below illustrates this structure.</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
